From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: swap chain frame statistics, background colour, rotation, source size, latency object, tearing, colour space, HDR metadata

These IDXGISwapChain1-4 methods were E_NOTIMPL stubs on the Direct3D 11 and
Direct3D 12 swap chains and half-done on the composition swap chain. They now
share one piece of bookkeeping (struct dxgi_swapchain_state).

GetFrameStatistics reports the present count, a refresh count taken from the
time since creation and the monitor's refresh rate, and the sync time.
Set/GetBackgroundColor, Set/GetRotation (1..4), Set/GetSourceSize (within the
buffers) store and validate. Set/GetMatrixTransform work for composition swap
chains and are DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL for window swap chains; the composition
swap chain applies source size, scale and offset when it draws.

DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_FLAG_FRAME_LATENCY_WAITABLE_OBJECT gives the D3D11 and
composition swap chains a real waitable object (a semaphore starting at the
maximum frame latency, given back by each present, resized by
SetMaximumFrameLatency). DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_FLAG_ALLOW_TEARING is accepted and
reported by GetDesc/GetDesc1; DXGI_PRESENT_ALLOW_TEARING needs the creation
flag and a sync interval of 0, else DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL. CheckColorSpaceSupport
and SetColorSpace1 accept only the sRGB colour space, SetHDRMetaData validates
its type and size, and the remaining FIXMEs (IsTemporaryMonoSupported,
GetRestrictToOutput, GetCoreWindow, GetCurrentBackBufferIndex) are gone.
